{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["And for the rear of the Tabernacle, to the west — these are the six boards placed at the western wall. Since the interior width of the Tabernacle is ten cubits, and the six western boards occupy only nine cubits from north to south, half a cubit of empty space remains at each of the two western corners, one on the north side and one on the south. The text therefore states ולמקצעעת המשכן תעשה שני קרשים — two corner boards, each a cubit and a half wide. One half-cubit of the first corner board fills the gap on the north side, while the remaining cubit of that same board extends along the western wall, covering the thickness of the northernmost board. Likewise, one half-cubit of the second corner board fills the gap on the south side, while the remaining cubit extends along the western wall, covering the thickness of the southernmost board. Thus you find the interior width of the Tabernacle to be exactly ten cubits, and the gaps at the corners are fully covered so that the exterior of the Tabernacle on all sides forms a perfect square."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The lemma in the source text appears to cite Exodus 26:23 (ולמקצעעת המשכן תעשה שני קרשים), embedded mid-comment rather than at the opening; I have rendered it as an integrated reference. The opening words 'ולירכתי המשכן תעשה ששה קרשים' appear to be Rashbam's own paraphrase of Exodus 26:22 rather than a verbatim lemma."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:16.030799230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}